                             LIBRARY POLICY SAYS:
                                       
   The ALA "Library Bill of Rights" says:
   
     A person's right to use a library should not be denied or abridged
     because of origin, age, background, or views.
     
   The ALA's "Free Access to Libraries for Minors" says:
   
     . . .[P]arents - and only parents - have the right and the
     responsibility to restrict the access of their children - and only
     their children - to library resources. [...] Librarians and
     governing bodies cannot assume the role of parents or the functions
     of parental authority in the private relationship between parent and
